+
+### Calling the evaluator from a thread pool
+
+The public `ParseEvaluator.evaluate(...)` may be called from a Python thread
+pool. Rule-based evaluation emits a `RuntimeWarning` when Unix main-thread
+alarms are unavailable. In that context, normalization and individual rules do
+**not** have a hard timeout. `BENCH_DOC_RULE_BUDGET_SECONDS` is still checked
+between rules, but cannot interrupt a rule or normalization that does not
+return. Putting a timeout on a thread future does not stop its underlying work.
+
+For untrusted documents or a required hard execution bound, run evaluation in
+an isolated process and enforce a process-level deadline. The standard
+`EvaluationRunner` evaluates in worker processes; on Unix their main threads
+retain the existing per-rule/normalization alarms. This thread-pool support does
+not change scoring, introduce another worker pool, or make thread execution a
+substitute for process isolation. Python subinterpreters are not covered by this
+thread-pool compatibility guarantee.
